media: cedrus: expose the H.264 hardware rotator

The H.264 secondary output combines power-of-two scale-down with clockwise
rotation.  Disassembly and hardware tests establish the mode bits for
0/90/180/270 degrees.  H.264 control bit 9 enables rotation when both scale
fields are zero, and 90/270 swap the output raster and stride.

Expose that unit through V4L2_CID_ROTATE.  Treat rotation like scaling for
private full-size reconstruction frames, capture allocation, format
selection and COMPOSE negotiation, so reference pictures never point at
transformed output.  Scale and rotation may be requested together.

A generated four-quadrant H.264 frame verified the output order for all
three angles and for half-scale plus 90 degrees on H713 hardware.

